{"additions":281,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNTc0OTIy","is_bot":false,"login":"cole-miller","name":"Cole Miller"},"body":"Before, `GlobalWatcher` held a native backend and a polling backend, and its methods dispatched to one or the other.\r\n\r\nAfter this PR, we have `OsWatcher` which wraps a single watch backend, and `RealFs` and `FakeFs` hold a native `OsWatcher` and a polling `OsWatcher`.\r\n\r\nThis moves the split closer to the place where we decide which backend should be used, and lets us clean up some indirection. A nice bonus is that the \"is this backend recursive\" data exists in exactly one place.\r\n\r\nRelease Notes:\r\n- N/A","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-07T19:49:19Z","deletions":352,"files":[{"path":"crates/fs/src/fs.rs","additions":25,"deletions":10,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/fs/src/fs_watcher.rs","additions":215,"deletions":311,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/recent_projects/src/dev_container_suggest.rs","additions":35,"deletions":31,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/recent_projects/src/recent_projects.rs","additions":6,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}],"isDraft":false,"labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOFExXwM8AAAABgYGhPg","name":"cla-signed","description":"The user has signed the Contributor License Agreement","color":"ededed"},{"id":"LA_kwDOFExXwM8AAAACXOSp6w","name":"staff","description":"Pull requests authored by a current member of Zed staff","color":"031c62"}],"mergedAt":"2026-09-07T20:45:31Z","number":63898,"reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDOFExXwM8AAAABMhQG6A","author":{"login":"Anthony-Eid"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T20:41:09Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"APPROVED","commit":{"oid":"72ef4568c9ffe257343ade0939c1fa37d9ef3199"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T20:25:57Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/actions/runs/34159382615/job/101857811761","name